t.getElementById('restart-btn').addEventListener('click', init);\n\ninit();\nrequestAnimationFrame(update);\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```","reasoning_content":"The user wants a complete Tetris game in a single HTML file. Let me write it carefully.\n\nRequirements: 10 cols × 20 rows, auto fall, left/right movement with collision, up rotation, down soft drop, space hard drop, 7 tetrominoes, line clear, score, next preview, game over overlay with restart.\n\nLet me write the code.\n\nGrid: array of 20 rows × 10 cols, null or color.\n\nTetromino shapes as matrices. Rotation with wall kicking simple.\n\nColors: I cyan, O yellow, T purple, S green, Z red, J blue, L orange.\n\nRender: canvas or DOM grid. Use canvas for simplicity. Draw next preview on a small canvas.\n\nGame loop with setInterval / requestAnimationFrame.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nLayout: title, two canvas areas, score, controls hint. Chinese UI fine (user wrote in Chinese).\n\nCode:\n\nconst COLS=10, ROWS=20;\nshapes: rotation via simple matrix rotation, check collision with bounds; if blocked try x offsets -1,1,2,-2.\n\nSpawn at top with y=0, x=3 (or 3 for most, adjust). Check collision -> game over.\n\nLock when can't move down after tick. Merge. Clear lines, add score (single 100, double 300, triple 500, tetris 800), speed up maybe.\n\nNext queue.\n\nHard drop: move down until blocked, add 2 per cell.\n\nSoft drop: per tick interval halved while key held — simplest: keydown on ArrowDown increases drop rate while held; use keys state.\n\nImplement loop with requestAnimationFrame timing.\n\nWrite the HTML."}}],"created":1795519785,"model":"/models/unsloth/Inkling-2-Mini-GGUF/Inkling-2-Mini-UD-Q3_K_XL.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b12651-d426a3774","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":4571,"prompt_tokens":318,"total_tokens":4889,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-aGGgUNyrcjjf3I7b2LlsABPWdNBG66ny","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":318,"prompt_ms":391.251,"prompt_pe